Backport of lxc/incus@ae5cb3a585de59c1d6183851f9e2629c1985a691 (stable-7.0; on main as
075b0944f) to v7.0.2 for the isx appliance (Sanne/incus-spawn#2739), unchanged: part of the fix
for GHSA-v855-hxm9-5pwg. A guest on the bridge could plant a malformed DHCP lease, with no Incus
API access, that crashed incusd whenever the leases were read. Remove this file once
INCUS_VERSION is a release that contains the commit (the next 7.0 release; 7.0.3 is not out
yet).

From ae5cb3a585de59c1d6183851f9e2629c1985a691 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?St=C3=A9phane=20Graber?= <stgraber@stgraber.org>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 19:57:45 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] incusd/network: Check the client ID length when parsing
 leases
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A lease with a short hardware address and a short client ID made the
parsers slice past the start of the column and panic, which took the
daemon down from the DNS server and the instance list.

This addresses GHSA-v855-hxm9-5pwg (CVE pending)

Signed-off-by: Stéphane Graber <stgraber@stgraber.org>
(cherry picked from commit ae5cb3a585de59c1d6183851f9e2629c1985a691)
---
 internal/server/network/driver_bridge.go | 3 ++-
 internal/server/network/network_utils.go | 3 ++-
 2 files changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/internal/server/network/driver_bridge.go b/internal/server/network/driver_bridge.go
index 271092b4c..48b75ac63 100644
--- a/internal/server/network/driver_bridge.go
+++ b/internal/server/network/driver_bridge.go
@@ -3484,7 +3484,8 @@ func (n *bridge) Leases(projectName string, clientType request.ClientType) ([]ap
 			mac := GetMACSlice(fields[1])
 			macStr := strings.Join(mac, ":")
 
-			if len(macStr) < 17 && fields[4] != "" {
+			// A short hardware address may be a DHCPv6 IAID, the MAC then ends the DUID.
+			if len(macStr) < 17 && len(fields[4]) >= 17 {
 				macStr = fields[4][len(fields[4])-17:]
 			}
 
diff --git a/internal/server/network/network_utils.go b/internal/server/network/network_utils.go
index e39ddf06c..e0b88b036 100644
--- a/internal/server/network/network_utils.go
+++ b/internal/server/network/network_utils.go
@@ -964,7 +964,8 @@ func GetLeaseAddresses(networkName string, hwaddr string) ([]net.IP, error) {
 		mac := GetMACSlice(fields[1])
 		macStr := strings.Join(mac, ":")
 
-		if len(macStr) < 17 && fields[4] != "" {
+		// A short hardware address may be a DHCPv6 IAID, the MAC then ends the DUID.
+		if len(macStr) < 17 && len(fields[4]) >= 17 {
 			macStr = fields[4][len(fields[4])-17:]
 		}
 
